KUSHAL(1)                     General Commands Manual                    KUSHAL(1)

NAME
     kushal — Kushal Gangarapu: grade 12, builds software his
     school actually runs on

SYNOPSIS
     kushal [--internship] [--coffee N] [--ship-it] problem...

DESCRIPTION
     The kushal utility takes a problem and attempts to solve it by
     shipping something a community will depend on, then supporting it
     at lunch the next day.

OPTIONS
     --internship     Seek summer 2027 internship. Currently active.
     --coffee N       Increase throughput by N cups. Diminishing returns
                      after N=3. Undefined behavior after N=6.
     --ship-it        Deploy to production where 1,500 people will find
                      the bug before you do. Frequently used.
     --hire           Print contact info. The good one.

ENVIRONMENT
     EDITOR           Set to kushal. Obviously.
     TABS_VS_SPACES   spaces. this is a safe space.
     SLEEP            Optional. Deprecated since student government.

FILES
     ~/.kushalrc      Sourced on login. Regretted on inspection.

BUGS
     Schedules hackathons during finals week.
     Checks the calendar's SSE dashboard from the cafeteria.
     Has never once said "it works" without adding "probably".

EXAMPLES
     kushal --internship        the whole reason you are here
     kushal --coffee 3          peak throughput, diminishing returns
     kushal --hire              see contact.env

REPORTING BUGS
     Bugs may be reported to contact.env. Complaints that the pep
     rally shows on the wrong day get same-day fixes — 1,500 users
     is a motivating audience.

SEE ALSO
     git(1), coffee(1), school(1)   — cannot exit any of them

AUTHORS
     Written and maintained by the same person. Reviews welcome.

